  "report": {
    "verdict": "dead",
    "why": "The Defender wins whatever the Attacker does. Expert against Expert, the Attacker wins 1.8% on the spec rules and 4.5% after the one allowed rule change (blockers tire), against the 30-70% role band; Expert also falls under 70% against Greedy (59.3%, then 65.5%) only because it cannot win as Attacker (20.5%, then 34%) while it wins 97-98% as Defender. Not the bot: Greedy against Greedy gives the Attacker 8% (14% with the change), and hold-then-strike Attacker plans did worse (0.3-4.5%) than attacking every round.",
    "loop": [
      "Attacker: deploy what the round number of mana buys, then send units; each unit sent into a Wall unit trades or dies, and only Climbers and unblocked overflow touch the Gate.",
      "Defender: block every sent unit it can, chump blocks included (a 1/3 Guard cancels a 4/6 Brute's whole hit), spend Oil and Snipes on the Field and Shooters on the 1-health Climbers, Repair when the Gate is down.",
      "Best play boils down to the Defender's fixed rule of blocking everything; Expert matches Greedy on 72% of decisions, and the Gate ends with 14 of 20 left on average between Experts.",
      "Costs bind: mana equals the round number, a card it could not afford sat in hand at 70% of turn ends, and a turn ended with mana and a playable card left at 18-29%."
    ]
  }
